\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Scheme of a single experimental repetition. Each dataset consists of 8 such repetitions, with atoms stacked between each run for the next cycle. The initial frequency $f_{0}$, the first microwave sweep of the $f_{c \rightarrow b}$scan, is determined by a low power scan to locate the "onset" of the transition. For subsequent repetitions, the starting frequency of each sweep is located is adjusted by subtracting the expected megnetic field drift.}}{18}{figure.3.3}\protected@file@percent }
